assertion  XSH.iswpunct.001
anchor     functions/iswpunct.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/iswpunct.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1.1
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1
class      required
says       In the POSIX locale iswpunct() returns non-zero for each character
           of the class punct as the locale definition lists it: the 32
           punctuation characters of the portable character set.
test       t/001-members.c

assertion  XSH.iswpunct.002
anchor     functions/iswpunct.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/iswpunct.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1.1
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1
class      required
says       In the POSIX locale iswpunct() returns 0 for each of these
           characters, which the locale definition does not place in the
           class: the letters, the digits, the space and the control
           characters.
test       t/002-non-members.c

assertion  XSH.iswpunct.003
anchor     functions/iswpunct.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/iswpunct.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
says       iswpunct(WEOF) is within the domain and returns 0, since WEOF is
           not a character of the class.
test       t/003-weof.c

assertion  XSH.iswpunct.004
anchor     functions/iswpunct.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/iswpunct.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1.1
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1
class      required
says       For each of the 128 characters, iswgraph() is non-zero exactly when
           iswalnum() or iswpunct() is non-zero, and no character has both
           iswpunct() and iswalnum() non-zero.
test       t/004-punct-with-alnum-is-graph.c
